<!-- Managed block: generated from the agent contract and the brain. Do not edit by hand; change the brain and regenerate. Text outside this block must not contradict the brain. -->

## Work on the brain

These rules apply to every change in `.brain/`, in addition to the managed block of the root instruction file.

- A new decision is a new file `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md` in `.brain/decisions/` (in the subdirectory the index's conventions name, if any) with frontmatter (`status`, `description`, and `decided` once resolved) and the sections its status requires, headed with labels from the `sections` map of the manifest. Before adding one, check the descriptions of existing decisions; if one already covers the matter, report it instead.
- After adding a decision or changing its frontmatter or title, regenerate `.brain/decisions/README.md`. After adding a document or changing its `description`, regenerate the index block in `.brain/README.md`. After changing the `status` or `assignee` of a step, regenerate its status line and the index block. Never edit generated views by hand.
- Resolve a conflict in a generated view by regenerating it. In the log of a step, keep the entries of both sides, sorted by date, with those already on the main branch first within a date. If a step added on your branch has the number of a step already on the main branch, give yours the first free number and fix the links to it. Resolve any other conflict in a document by reading both versions and the version before the change; merge what does not contradict, and record a contradiction as a `proposed` decision with both options. If a decision accepted on your branch contradicts one accepted on the main branch, turn yours back to `proposed` as that decision; until it is resolved, the main branch's version binds.
- When the work on a step starts, set its `status` to `in-progress` and its `assignee` to the people doing the work (in the first commit of the work). Do a step with `stages` one stage at a time, each leaving the work in a working state (one commit each). Record progress in its log, one list entry per change or finished stage, starting with the date (`- YYYY-MM-DD: …`).
- Keep raw material (recordings, transcripts, emails, PDFs, contracts, images) at its source: write to the brain what follows from it (decisions, knowledge, open questions) with a link to the source, never the material itself.
- Do not put run instructions, commands, personal notes or personal data into the brain; commands go to the repository's `README.md` or outside the managed blocks of instruction files.
- If the `dotbrain` CLI is available, run `dotbrain lint` before ending work that changed the brain, and fix what it reports.
<!-- END:dotbrain -->
-- .brain/README.md --
---
brain: notes-api
lang: en
spec: 1.0.0
owner: ana
description: "Source of truth for the Notes API: the service that stores notes for the Notes apps."
---
# Notes API

The Notes API stores the notes of the Notes web and mobile apps. The brain is the source of truth for its product, architecture, infrastructure and code: a decision is made here first, then carried into the code, and a change that departs from a document updates it in the same pull request.

<!-- BEGIN:dotbrain index -->
<!-- Generated from document frontmatter. Do not edit by hand; regenerate on conflict. -->

- [risks.md](risks.md): Risks of the Notes API with their impact and mitigation.
- [roadmap.md](roadmap.md): Phases of the Notes API and the gates between them.

`architecture/`:

- [overview.md](architecture/overview.md): Architecture of the Notes API: components, data and hosting.

`decisions/`:

- [decisions/README.md](decisions/README.md): Decisions: Proposed, Accepted, Rejected, Superseded

`steps/`:

- [01-walking-skeleton.md](steps/01-walking-skeleton.md): A deployed API that creates, lists and deletes notes. (`in-progress`)
- [02-sharing.md](steps/02-sharing.md): Notes shared with other users. (`draft`)
<!-- END:dotbrain index -->

## Steps

Phases of the [roadmap](roadmap.md) are split into steps in `steps/NN-short-name.md`. A step is the spec the work is done by; its status is in the frontmatter (`draft`, `agreed`, `in-progress`, `done`).

## Conventions

- Decisions are in subdirectories of `decisions/` by domain (`decisions/<domain>/`), such as `process/` for the rules of work. A domain is a short English name in kebab-case. A new domain is created when a decision fits none of the existing ones; a decision that concerns several domains goes to the one where it has the most effect.
-- .brain/architecture/overview.md --
---
description: "Architecture of the Notes API: components, data and hosting."
---
# Overview

The API is one service in front of one database.

## Data

Notes are rows with an owner, a body and the timestamps `created_at`, `updated_at` and `deleted_at`.
-- .brain/decisions/README.md --
---
description: "Decisions: Proposed, Accepted, Rejected, Superseded"
---
# Decisions

<!-- Generated from decision frontmatter. Do not edit by hand; regenerate on conflict. -->

## Proposed

- [Database for notes](data/2026-11-03-database.md): Whether notes are stored in SQLite or in PostgreSQL.

## Accepted

- [Languages of the work](process/2026-11-01-languages.md): Code, identifiers, comments, log and error messages, commits, branch names and pull requests are in English. (2026-11-01)
- [Brain changes with the work](process/2026-11-01-order-of-work.md): Changes to the brain go in the same pull request as the work that follows from them. (2026-11-01)
- [Hosting on Fly.io](infrastructure/2026-11-02-hosting-on-fly-io.md): The API runs on Fly.io, in one region close to most users. (2026-11-02)
- [Soft delete of notes](api/2026-11-02-soft-delete.md): Deleting a note sets `deleted_at` instead of removing the row. (2026-11-02)

## Rejected

- [GraphQL endpoint](api/2026-11-02-graphql-endpoint.md): The API does not offer GraphQL; it stays REST only. (2026-11-02)

## Superseded

- [Hosting on Heroku](infrastructure/2026-10-30-hosting-on-heroku.md): The API runs on Heroku. (2026-10-30) → [2026-11-02-hosting-on-fly-io](infrastructure/2026-11-02-hosting-on-fly-io.md)
-- .brain/decisions/api/2026-11-02-graphql-endpoint.md --
---
status: rejected
decided: 2026-11-02
description: "The API does not offer GraphQL; it stays REST only."
---
# GraphQL endpoint

## Decision

Rejected: the apps need only a few fixed queries, and one style of API is enough.
-- .brain/decisions/api/2026-11-02-soft-delete.md --
---
status: accepted
decided: 2026-11-02
apply: ["src/notes/**", "*.sql"]
description: "Deleting a note sets `deleted_at` instead of removing the row."
---
# Soft delete of notes

## Context

Users restore notes deleted by mistake, and support needs the history of a note.

## Decision

Deleting a note sets `deleted_at` instead of removing the row, and a deleted note answers `404`. Queries and migrations filter on `deleted_at` ([overview](../../architecture/overview.md#data)).
-- .brain/decisions/data/2026-11-03-database.md --
---
status: proposed
description: "Whether notes are stored in SQLite or in PostgreSQL."
---
# Database for notes

## Context

The first release needs a database. The team has used both.

## Options

1. **SQLite:** one file, no server, easy backups; limited concurrent writes.
2. **PostgreSQL:** a managed service on the host; one more service to run.

## Recommendation

PostgreSQL, because the host offers it managed.

## Who decides and when

Ana, before step 1 is done.
-- .brain/decisions/infrastructure/2026-10-30-hosting-on-heroku.md --
---
status: superseded
decided: 2026-10-30
superseded-by: 2026-11-02-hosting-on-fly-io
description: "The API runs on Heroku."
---
# Hosting on Heroku

## Decision

The API runs on one Heroku dyno with Heroku Postgres.
-- .brain/decisions/infrastructure/2026-11-02-hosting-on-fly-io.md --
---
status: accepted
decided: 2026-11-02
description: "The API runs on Fly.io, in one region close to most users."
---
# Hosting on Fly.io

## Context

Replaces [hosting on Heroku](2026-10-30-hosting-on-heroku.md): the free tier ended.

## Decision

The API runs on Fly.io in one region close to most users, with a managed Postgres.
-- .brain/decisions/process/2026-11-01-languages.md --
